cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use fishladder in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "fishladder: an evaluation framework for online multi-output active learning on data streams"
abstract: >-
  fishladder is a Python library to evaluate active learning methods on
  multi-output data streams, where each output has its own labelling cost and
  delay. It provides query strategies, budgets, prequential evaluation with
  delayed labels, randomized querying and a synthetic multi-target stream
  generator, and follows the conventions of River.
